# WLISTTO.KEY - the scroll bar of a list of three rows in a 2-row window,
# counted exactly by the survey after the first page: range 0 to 1;
# TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WLISTTO.SNP.  The title is "what #n p/m c": n the busy
# moves, p and m the bar's position and range top, c the count.
S START
# A line down within the window moves the selection alone and is not
# busy; the next leaves the window and moves the bar; a third, at the
# last row, is busy and stays.
K D
S LDOWN1
K D
S LDOWN2
K D
S LDOWN3
K U
S LUP1
K U
S LUP2
# A page down, a page up, the bottom and the top.
K N
S PGDN
K P
S PGUP
K B
S BOTTOM
K T
S TOP
# CTRL: the gesture twice, the second ending while the first's move is
# posted, so dropped: one line down, within the window, not busy.
K CTRL-D
S CDOWN
K CTRL-U
S CUP
# X, a line down then a page up in one gesture: the page up alone.
K B
K X
S KIND
# L, a line down whose gesture never ends, is lost: the next key's line
# down moves one row, within the window.
K L
S LOST
K D
S LOSTD
# G posts a line down, then moves to the end, whose walk dispatches the
# gesture while busy: dropped, the End move alone counts.
K T
K G
S BUSYG
# The thumb released where it was makes no move; dragged to the top, a
# jump to row 0; to the bottom, the End move.
K 1
S THUMB1
K 0
S THUMB0
K 0
S THUMB00
K 1
S THUMBEND
# A lead row counts in the range but not in the count.
K CTRL-F4
S LEAD
K 2
S LEADEND
K 1
S LEADMID
K 0
S LEADTOP
